  "description": "Merged 13 ibm security advisories published on 2026-09-01. Original advisory IDs: IBM-7285911, IBM-7285930, IBM-7285931, IBM-7285507, IBM-7285988, IBM-7285987, IBM-7286010, IBM-7286012, IBM-7286014, IBM-7286011, IBM-7285897, IBM-7284501, IBM-7284498\n\nTitles:\n- security vulnerabilities are addressed with IBM Business Automation Insights iFixes for August 2026.\n- Multiple secuirty vulnerabilies addressed with IBM Business Automation Workflow August 2026\n- Multiple security vulnerabilities are addressed with IBM Cloud Pak for Business Automation iFixes for August 2026.\n- Vulnerabilities exists in IBM Cloud Pak for Data System (CPDS 1.0)\n- Security vulnerability in IBM WebSphere Application Server Liberty affects IBM Robotic Process Automation and IBM Robotic Process Automation for Cloud Pak\n- Security vulnerability in Python affects  IBM Robotic Process Automation and IBM Robotic Process Automation for Cloud Pak\n- IBM QRadar SIEM contains components with known vulnerabilities\n- IBM QRadar SIEM could allow an authenticated user to obtain sensitive information from backup files due to incorrect permissions assignment.\n- Multiple vulnerabilities found in logback-core jar which is part of IBM webMethods  API Management\n- IBM Storage Fusion Data Foundation is vulnerable to Authorization Bypass.\n- IBM Storage Fusion Data Foundation is vulnerable to Security Bypass",
